<title>USA: Delaware plan to raise gas tax resurfaces.</title>
<headline>Delaware plan to raise gas tax resurfaces.</headline>
<dateline>DOVER, Del. 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A proposal to increase Delaware's gas tax has resurfaced, with Sen. Tom Sharp arguing that the idea could fund transportation projects.</p>
<p>Gov. Tom Carper abandoned the gas tax plan earlier in the legislative session, and House Majority Leader Wayne Smith said many Republicans in the state are still opposed to the idea.</p>
<p>The plan originally called for a four-cent increase. But Sharp said a one- or two-cent increase in the tax could be enough to fund transportation projects under consideration.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
